From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 17:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] The field's ground and buildings not sent in frames not shown (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Faster than 1x (the 3DS remaster's SPEED option) the game runs several
frames for each one shown, and every frame of the field made its whole
3D scene: at 4x two a V-blank, one of them never seen. In a town that
was most of the game's core (Sandgem: 3 ms a halt against 0.5 indoors,
12 ms of each V-blank's 16.7), the display thread below it there got to
compose the screens 20 times a second, and the game itself ran between
150 and 240 frames a second ("sluggish", "skipping frames", a tester's
log of 2026-11-10).

The port now says which frames' scenes will be shown
(NitroPort_FieldSceneWanted) and leaves the others' out. In a frame
whose scene is left out the field doesn't send its ground or its
buildings (LandDataManager_RenderLoadedMaps, MapPropManager_Render2:
most of the work, and nothing but drawing). Everything else in the frame
runs as before: the people's and the field effects' drawing and what
they keep count of, the Poké Radar's check, the tasks the field draws
from, the request to swap. At 1x every scene is wanted, and in the
Distortion World it's never asked.
---
diff --git a/src/overlay005/fieldmap.c b/src/overlay005/fieldmap.c
--- a/src/overlay005/fieldmap.c
+++ b/src/overlay005/fieldmap.c
@@ -139,6 +139,9 @@
 static enum FieldExtensionOverlay FieldMap_GetExtOverlayForActiveDynMapFeatures(FieldSystem *fieldSystem);
 static BOOL FieldMap_InDistortionWorld(FieldSystem *fieldSystem);
 #ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+// 1: this frame's 3D scene will be shown; 0, faster than 1x: it won't
+// (3ds_port/nitro/include/nitro_port_speed.h).
+extern int NitroPort_FieldSceneWanted(void);
 static void FieldMap_PortNeighbours(FieldSystem *fieldSystem);
 static void FieldMap_PortLogUnseen(FieldSystem *fieldSystem);
 static void FieldMap_PortKeepHiddenInSight(FieldSystem *fieldSystem, enum MapHeaderID mapHeaderID, int objEventCount, const ObjectEvent *objEventList);
@@ -743,6 +746,20 @@
     }
 
     PokeRadar_ClearIfAllOutOfView(fieldSystem);
+
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+    // Faster than 1x (the options page's SPEED) the game runs several
+    // frames for each one shown. A frame that won't be shown made its whole
+    // scene all the same: in a town at 4x the ground and the buildings sent
+    // twice a V-blank took most of the game's core, and the screens came
+    // 20 times a second for it. Such a frame's scene is left out by the
+    // port (NitroPort_Gx3dLeaveOut), so its ground and buildings, most of
+    // the work and nothing but drawing, aren't sent at all. The rest of the
+    // frame is as ever: the people's and the effects' drawing with what
+    // they keep count of, the Poké Radar's check, the tasks drawn from. Not
+    // in the Distortion World (never asked there: every scene made).
+    if (FieldMap_InDistortionWorld(fieldSystem) == TRUE || NitroPort_FieldSceneWanted()) {
+#endif
     LandDataManager_RenderLoadedMaps(fieldSystem->landDataMan, fieldSystem->areaModelAttrs);
 
     if (FieldMap_InDistortionWorld(fieldSystem) == TRUE) {
@@ -750,6 +767,9 @@
     }
 
     MapPropManager_Render2(fieldSystem->mapPropManager, fieldSystem->areaDataManager);
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+    }
+#endif
 
     {
         const MtxFx44 *v2;
-- 
2.43.0

